# Settings for scripts/chain/run.sh: copy to ~/.config/filex-chain.env (or
# pass --env FILE). KEY=VALUE, no expansion; the process environment wins
# over this file. Every key is optional.

# Where runs, caches and the default lock live.
CHAIN_ROOT=/var/lib/filex-chain
# The lock every build on this host takes (`none`: no lock). run.sh waits for
# it as long as it takes, or CHAIN_LOCK_WAIT_MIN minutes when the PROCESS
# environment sets that (run.sh reads no file; it exits 3 when the time is up).
# CHAIN_LOCK=/var/lib/filex-chain/lock
# Names of the containers, networks and sidecars (one run per prefix at a time).
# CHAIN_PREFIX=fxchain

# Memory, in GiB. The most the chain's jobs may hold at once (by the memory
# each was measured to hold, scripts/chain/plan.mjs WEIGHTS), and the
# MemAvailable the run and each job leave free. A run takes CHAIN_MEM_GB, or
# less when the host has less: MemAvailable at its start less
# CHAIN_MEM_RESERVE_GB (chain.log names the containers that are not the
# chain's and what they hold). A smaller budget makes a run longer, not red.
# CHAIN_MEM_GB=8
# CHAIN_MEM_RESERVE_GB=1
# CHAIN_POOL_MAX=3
# CHAIN_CPUS=12
# vitest forks in the web job (0: vitest's default, one per core but one).
# CHAIN_WEB_WORKERS=8

# What else the host runs, out of the run's way. Once the lock is held, and
# before the run measures MemAvailable, run.sh runs CHAIN_PAUSE_CMD (with
# `bash -c`); when that exits 0, it runs CHAIN_RESUME_CMD once when the run
# ends - green, red, a setup error or stopped by a signal - with the run's exit
# code in CHAIN_EXIT. Each may take CHAIN_HOOK_TIMEOUT_S seconds (0: no limit),
# runs in a process group of its own, with no terminal and without the lock's
# file descriptor. A pause that fails or times out is in chain.log and
# result.json `host.pause`; the run goes on beside what it was to pause, and
# nothing is resumed. One line each, a command on THIS host - no secret in it:
# a script that reads its own settings. For example an Android emulator that
# holds 3-4 GiB: the pause shuts it down cleanly, the resume starts it again
# and waits until it has booted. Unset (the default): nothing runs.
# CHAIN_PAUSE_CMD=/usr/local/lib/chain-hooks/emulator-pause.sh
# CHAIN_RESUME_CMD=/usr/local/lib/chain-hooks/emulator-resume.sh
# CHAIN_HOOK_TIMEOUT_S=900

# The host's pressure. The pool starts no job while the kernel says the host
# is stalled (PSI "full", avg10, a fraction of the time; 0 turns a check off),
# for at most CHAIN_PSI_WAIT_MIN minutes at a time, and starts one job per
# CHAIN_START_GAP_S seconds so that the next sees what the last one did.
# CHAIN_PSI_MEM_MAX=0.1
# CHAIN_PSI_IO_MAX=0.4
# CHAIN_PSI_WAIT_MIN=5
# CHAIN_START_GAP_S=20
# The disk whose write latency the run records (a /proc/diskstats name;
# default: the one CHAIN_ROOT is on).
# CHAIN_DISK=dm-0
# The /tmp of a Go test job and e2e/test-results of a Playwright line (every
# test's trace and video, deleted when it passes) are each a tmpfs of at most
# this many GiB (0: on the disk), so neither goes to the disk.
# CHAIN_TMPFS_GB=3

# Caches shared between runs (default: $CHAIN_ROOT/cache/...). The Go jobs
# run as CHAIN_GO_USER (default 1000:1000) with CHAIN_GOCACHE, the build as
# root with CHAIN_GOCACHE_ROOT; one directory serves both only when its
# subdirectories already belong to that user.
# CHAIN_GOMODCACHE=  CHAIN_GOCACHE=  CHAIN_GOCACHE_ROOT=  CHAIN_PNPM_STORE=
# CHAIN_CYPRESS_CACHE=  CHAIN_ELECTRON_CACHE=  CHAIN_HOME=  CHAIN_GOROOT=
# CHAIN_GO_USER=1000:1000

# Images (defaults: the Playwright of pnpm-lock.yaml, the Go of
# backend/go.mod, the S3 gateway e2e/lib/s3server.mjs pins).
# CHAIN_DS_IMAGE=onlyoffice/documentserver:latest
# CHAIN_PW_IMAGE=  CHAIN_GO_IMAGE=  CHAIN_NODE_IMAGE=  CHAIN_S3_IMAGE=
# CHAIN_PG_IMAGE=  CHAIN_MYSQL_IMAGE=  CHAIN_REDIS_IMAGE=  CHAIN_SMB_IMAGE=
# The Document Server's own network (a free /24 on this host).
# CHAIN_DS_SUBNET=172.30.81.0/24

# The app builds the browser suite installs, and the shots job's app scenes
# (all but lang-ar, the suite's right-to-left fixture). A spec whose build is
# missing is red (FILEX_REQUIRE_WASM_FIXTURE=1, as on CI), and so is the
# shots job; CHAIN_REQUIRE_APPS=0 lets those specs skip and the shots job
# leave the app and Document Server scenes out instead.
# CHAIN_SIGN_APP_DIR=/path/to/filex-sign/dist
# CHAIN_CONVERT_APP_DIR=/path/to/filex-convert
# CHAIN_LANG_ES_DIR=/path/to/filex-lang-es
# CHAIN_LANG_DE_DIR=/path/to/filex-lang-de
# CHAIN_LANG_FR_DIR=/path/to/filex-lang-fr
# CHAIN_LANG_AR_DIR=/path/to/filex-lang-ar
# CHAIN_REQUIRE_APPS=1

# A disk that throttles when hot: before every Playwright job the chain waits
# (at most CHAIN_TEMP_WAIT_MIN, and CHAIN_TEMP_WAIT_TOTAL_MIN in a whole run)
# until this Prometheus query is at most CHAIN_TEMP_MAX degrees. Ask for THIS
# host's drive and for the sensor its thresholds are on: an NVMe drive
# throttles on its Composite temperature (warning at 82.85 C on the build
# host's), while another of its sensors can read 85-90 C under any load, and
# a query over every host's sensors waits for the hottest machine.
# CHAIN_TEMP_PROM=http://127.0.0.1:9090
# CHAIN_TEMP_QUERY=max(node_hwmon_temp_celsius{instance="buildhost",chip=~"nvme.*"} * on(instance, chip, sensor) group_left node_hwmon_sensor_label{label="Composite"})
# CHAIN_TEMP_MAX=75
# CHAIN_TEMP_WAIT_TOTAL_MIN=30

# Where the end of a run is posted: a JSON POST with a Bearer key read from
# CHAIN_NOTIFY_KEY_FILE (never logged). Unset = no post.
# CHAIN_NOTIFY_URL=https://notify.example.com/api/notify/v1/send
# CHAIN_NOTIFY_KEY_FILE=/var/lib/filex-chain/notify.key
# CHAIN_NOTIFY_GROUP=infra
# CHAIN_NOTIFY_SOURCE=filex-chain

# The nightly profile's extras (ds-go, s3-live, shots, realenv) and the
# nightly run that starts it: scripts/chain/nightly.env.example (s3-live's
# FILEX_TEST_S3_* settings are there too).
# CHAIN_NIGHTLY_EXTRAS=ds-go,s3-live,shots,realenv
# The same extras on a targeted run, by name (none by default): s3-live with
# FILEX_TEST_S3_* is the live S3 tests by hand (scripts/chain/nightly.mjs s3-live),
# shots a release's pictures.
# CHAIN_EXTRAS=s3-live
# The shots job takes every scene (pnpm shots --all); these shot scripts
# instead (comma-separated, without .mjs).
# CHAIN_SHOTS_ONLY=apps,signing

# Other lists: a path, or cmd:<command> whose output is a list in the same
# format. The Go and -race jobs default to the shards of
# scripts/test-shards.json (cmd:node scripts/test-shards.mjs go --profile
# go|race --format chain), the browser round to scripts/chain/lists/e2e.txt.
# CHAIN_GO_LIST=  CHAIN_RACE_LIST=  CHAIN_E2E_LIST=
